# vector_add_float16b.cbtable
#   The three circular buffers vector_add uses, written out as a real CB table instead
#   of inherited from build_tensix_kernel.sh's legacy uniform default. Same shape as
#   that default -- 32x32 Float16_b, 4 faces, 2048 B a tile -- so a build driven by this
#   file must produce the same descriptors, and the same kernel, as one driven by no
#   file at all. That equality is the control for the Float32 table beside it.
#
#   CB indices match vector_add's compile-time args: 0 and 1 in, 16 out.
#
#   Format: tools/emit_tensix_cb_formats.py
#   cb <index> <format> <tile_r> <tile_c> <face_r> <num_faces>

math_fidelity  4
approx         0
dst_accum_mode 0

cb  0  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb  1  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
cb 16  Float16_b 32 32 16 4
